+
+### Korean SAF Documents Provider (app-private files, user-granted access)
+
+`AppFilesDocumentsProvider.kt` registers `${applicationId}.documents` as a system SAF `DocumentsProvider`, with the Android `MANAGE_DOCUMENTS` binding permission and URI grants. The exposed root is **`filesDir` only** (`files/`), not the app's private SharedPreferences/databases/cache or `/data/data` generally. Android's file picker mediates all third-party document grants; files are not globally readable.
+
+`AppDocumentsPath.kt` is the single source of truth for stable `files:` document IDs, canonical containment and symlink/traversal rejection; `AppDocumentsPathTest.kt` tests identity, unsafe names, path escapes and the SAF manifest declaration. Direct edits through the file picker can still change/delete engine data: warn users to back up before changing the runtime, and do not recursively delete directories from the provider. The UI language dialog remains `GuideManagementController.kt` and the selected locale source remains `AppLanguage.kt`.
